Cloudstic — Content-Addressable Backup System

COMMAND
  cloudstic list [options]
  List all backup snapshots in the repository

OPTIONS
    -group                         Group snapshots by source identity

GLOBAL OPTIONS (also settable via environment variables)
    -config-dir <path>             Directory for profiles, tokens, and other state  [env: CLOUDSTIC_CONFIG_DIR]
    -no-prompt                     Disable interactive prompts (for scripts and CI)
    -store <uri>                   Storage backend URI: local:<path>, s3:<bucket>[/<prefix>], b2:<bucket>[/<prefix>], sftp://[user@]host[:port]/<path>  [env: CLOUDSTIC_STORE]
    -profile <name>                Profile name from profiles.yaml  [env: CLOUDSTIC_PROFILE]
    -profiles-file <path>          Path to profiles YAML file  [env: CLOUDSTIC_PROFILES_FILE]
    -s3-endpoint <url>             S3 compatible endpoint URL (for MinIO, R2, etc.)  [env: CLOUDSTIC_S3_ENDPOINT]
    -s3-region <region>            S3 region (default us-east-1)  [env: CLOUDSTIC_S3_REGION]
    -s3-profile <name>             AWS shared config profile for S3 credentials  [env: CLOUDSTIC_S3_PROFILE]
    -s3-access-key <key>           S3 access key ID  [env: AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID]
    -s3-secret-key <secret>        S3 secret access key  [env: AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY]
    -b2-key-id <key-id>            Backblaze B2 application key ID  [env: B2_KEY_ID]
    -b2-app-key <key>              Backblaze B2 application key  [env: B2_APP_KEY]
    -disable-packfile              Disable bundling small objects into 8MB packs  [env: CLOUDSTIC_DISABLE_PACKFILE]
    -store-sftp-password <pw>      SFTP store password  [env: CLOUDSTIC_STORE_SFTP_PASSWORD]
    -store-sftp-key <path>         Path to SSH private key for SFTP store  [env: CLOUDSTIC_STORE_SFTP_KEY]
    -store-sftp-insecure           Skip host key validation for SFTP store (INSECURE)  [env: CLOUDSTIC_STORE_SFTP_INSECURE]
    -store-sftp-known-hosts <path> Path to known_hosts file for SFTP store  [env: CLOUDSTIC_STORE_SFTP_KNOWN_HOSTS]
    -password <pw>                 Repository password  [env: CLOUDSTIC_PASSWORD]
    -encryption-key <hex>          Platform key (hex-encoded, 32 bytes)  [env: CLOUDSTIC_ENCRYPTION_KEY]
    -recovery-key <words>          Recovery key (BIP39 24-word mnemonic)  [env: CLOUDSTIC_RECOVERY_KEY]
    -kms-key-arn <arn>             AWS KMS key ARN for kms-platform slots  [env: CLOUDSTIC_KMS_KEY_ARN]
    -kms-region <region>           AWS KMS region (default: from AWS environment)  [env: CLOUDSTIC_KMS_REGION]
    -kms-endpoint <url>            Custom AWS KMS endpoint URL  [env: CLOUDSTIC_KMS_ENDPOINT]
    -prompt                        Prompt for password interactively (use alongside --encryption-key or --kms-key-arn to add a password layer)
    -verbose                       Log detailed file-level operations
    -quiet                         Suppress progress bars (keeps final summary)
    -json                          Write command result as JSON to stdout
    -debug                         Log every store request (network calls, timing, sizes)

